                                ['type' => 'explanation', 'title' => 'Cutting and replacing', 'body' => "Ellipsis after auxiliaries — keep the auxiliary, drop the rest:\n- \"Can you attend?\" — \"I can't, but Rani can.\"\n- \"He hasn't finished, but he will [finish] by noon.\"\n\nSubstitution with do so / do / one(s):\n- \"Asked to justify the cut, the minister declined to do so.\"\n- \"These figures are outdated; the ones from March are reliable.\"\n\nSo / not after believe, hope, suppose, be afraid:\n- \"Will the flight be delayed?\" — \"I'm afraid so.\" / \"I hope not.\"\n\nIf/whether clauses reduce too: \"Attend if you can [attend].\" \"He'll object — he always does.\"", 'body_id' => 'Elipsis: pertahankan kata bantu, buang sisanya ("I can\'t, but Rani can"). Substitusi: "do so" menggantikan kata kerja + objek, "one/ones" menggantikan kata benda, dan "so/not" menggantikan klausa setelah hope/afraid/suppose ("I hope not").'],
